{"author":{"id":"1d21e70a32f794e19f8d3626c963a95c52102f79bd1dc44e2b4b611903f1b863"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780989847,"nonce":"DXmFh9PIZX4hTgDT/LJRnd0kYo8=","title":"The Perfect Commit","message":"Ideally each commit should package implementation, tests, documentation, and a link to the issue.\n\n\nThis feels kind of difficult for Nix config - we can configure NixOS VM tests at most.\n\n\nThe repo should definitely include a `docs/` or `wiki/` directory that is updated alongside the implementations as a reference and guide for what was added.\nNote that this should be human-written as much as possible primarily to avoid overly verbose documentation.\n\n\nI tried using Linear but it's too much friction to have to go to the Web UI and such. I am trying out git-bug in the `the-perfect-commit` branch.\n\n- https://simonwillison.net/2022/Oct/29/the-perfect-commit","files":null}]}